  "cross_sdk": {
    "description": "A pending_calls record uses the same keys and value types in the three SDKs: matched, usage_known, and started_at / ended_at in epoch milliseconds. Each snapshot holds the same two calls recorded during paused-response delivery with emitLlmCalls on, as its written_by SDK writes them: a span with known usage and a wrapper call with unknown usage, both unmatched and timed. The two entries marked before SDK-6111 use the keys Python (started_ns, ended_ns) and Go (twin_matched, usage_unknown, RFC 3339 times) wrote until then, which every reader still accepts. For each snapshot: restore it with emitLlmCalls on, record reports in order (source wrapper or span, started_ms / ended_ms in epoch milliseconds), then end. Each report merges into its pending twin in the restored run, so expected.response is a subset of the final ai_response_received and expected.call_events lists a subset of each ai_llm_response_received, in order. Each SDK also writes the scenario itself and compares its pending_calls with its own entry.",
